-- title:
--   Centre of a valuation ring passes between the Igusa charts
-- statement:
--   Fix a natural number $M \ne 0$ and a prime $\ell$, and write $F = \mathtt{modularFunctionFieldFull } M$ for the subfield of the Laurent series field $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the expansions $\mathtt{qExpand } \mathbb{Q}\, d\, jq$ for the divisors $d$ of $M$. Over the coefficient ring [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt ℓ`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) let $A = \mathtt{chartAlgFin } M\, \ell$ be the subalgebra of $F$ of elements integral over the subalgebra generated by $j$ (the element `IgusaScheme.jFull M`), and $A_\infty = \mathtt{chartAlgInf } M\, \ell$ the subalgebra of elements integral over the subalgebra generated by $j^{-1}$. Let $\mathfrak q$ be a prime of $A$ and $\mathfrak r$ a prime of $A_\infty$ whose images under the morphisms `IgusaScheme.ιFin M ℓ` and `IgusaScheme.ιInf M ℓ` into the Igusa scheme — the pushout of $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the two inclusions of the overlap algebra into $A$ and into $A_\infty$ — agree as points. Let $V$ be a valuation subring of $F$ such that every element of $A_\infty$ lies in $V$, and such that for $b \in A_\infty$ one has $b \in \mathfrak r$ if and only if $b$ is a non-unit of $V$. The conclusion is the same description of $\mathfrak q$: for every $a \in A$, $a \in \mathfrak q$ if and only if $a$ is a non-unit of $V$, i.e. $\mathfrak q = A \cap \mathfrak m_V$.
--
--   The statement says that a valuation subring of the modular function field which is centred at $\mathfrak r$ on the pole chart $A_\infty$ is also centred at $\mathfrak q$ on the finite chart $A$, whenever $\mathfrak q$ and $\mathfrak r$ are the two chart-descriptions of one point of the two-chart Igusa model. It is used in [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.exists_fst_comp_zero_genericPoint_eq_iotaFin_and_mem_asIdeal_iff`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.exists_fst_comp_zero_genericPoint_eq_iotaFin_and_mem_asIdeal_iff), where the valuation subring is the one produced for the model package.
